await put('05_dialogue/DIALOGUE_SYSTEM_REPORT.md',`# Dialogue system report\n\n1. Dialogue starts when renderCase loads a case and app.js selects runtimeDialogue.cases[id].lines.\n2. The visible component is #dialogue inside .dialogue-strip; #speaker identifies the role.\n3. Data is in data/runtime-dialogue.json; authored source is data/case-dialogues.json.\n4. The opening line is lines[0]; follow-up phases use lines[1], [2], [3], and [4].\n5. Runtime choices: ${dChoices.length}; authored cases: ${runtime.cases.length}.\n6. A choice calls addTag(tag), changing tags/evidence and sometimes route relationships/reputation.\n7. follow-up selection uses state.dialoguePhase and the current case line index in the final advance wrapper.\n8. A case ends after the three dialogue choices and moves to the next case or E07.\n9. Next scene trigger is advance() / renderCase() / renderScene('E07'); final ending uses showEnding().\n10. Evidence metadata is present on runtime lines ('evidence_class', 'source_ids', 'voice_profile') but the source-reading UI reuses line.text as translation in the sampled adapter path.\n\nSee DIALOGUE_EXAMPLES.md for 10 exports from actual runtime lines and choices.\n`);
